{
  "mn105:0.1": "Middle Discourses 105 ",
  "mn105:0.2": "With Sunakkhatta ",
  "mn105:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn105:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Vesālī, at the Great Wood, in the hall with the peaked roof. ",
  "mn105:2.1": "Now at that time several mendicants had declared their enlightenment in the Buddha’s presence: ",
  "mn105:2.2": "“We understand: ‘Rebirth is ended, the spiritual journey has been completed, what had to be done has been done, there is nothing further for this place.’” ",
  "mn105:2.3": "Sunakkhatta the Licchavi heard about this. ",
  "mn105:2.4": "",
  "mn105:2.5": "",
  "mn105:3.1": "He went to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him, ",
  "mn105:4.1": "“Sir, I have heard that ",
  "mn105:4.2": "several mendicants have declared their enlightenment in the Buddha’s presence. ",
  "mn105:4.3": "",
  "mn105:4.4": "",
  "mn105:4.5": "I trust they did so rightly—or are there some who declared enlightenment out of overestimation?” ",
  "mn105:5.1": "",
  "mn105:5.2": "",
  "mn105:5.3": "“Some of them did so rightly, Sunakkhatta, while others did so out of overestimation. ",
  "mn105:5.4": "Now, when mendicants declare enlightenment rightly, that is their truth. ",
  "mn105:5.5": "But when mendicants declare enlightenment out of overestimation, the Realized One thinks: ",
  "mn105:5.6": "‘I should teach them the Dhamma.’ ",
  "mn105:5.7": "If the Realized One thinks ",
  "mn105:5.8": "he should teach them the Dhamma, ",
  "mn105: